\begin{equation*}
136w- 203k = 184 = 2^3 \cdot  23.
\end{equation*}
But the gcd of 136 and 203 is 1, as noted previously. Therefore, the integer solutions for $w$ that satisfy $184 \mod 203$ are such that
\begin{equation*}
w \equiv 114, 112 \mod{203}.
\end{equation*}

